WEBVTT

00:00:02.600 --> 00:00:13.250
Spring is in the air, and the season for cherry blossoms has arrived.

00:00:13.250 --> 00:00:18.170
The new year once again brings us youth with shining futures.

00:00:18.170 --> 00:00:22.620
Isn't it wonderful?

00:00:22.620 --> 00:00:28.960
It is not only our duty, but also our joy,

00:00:28.960 --> 00:00:39.070
to properly bring up these youths, full of hope, who now enter our school.

00:00:40.460 --> 00:00:41.750
You called?

00:00:41.750 --> 00:00:43.460
Yes, come in.

00:00:44.570 --> 00:00:46.570
Um...

00:00:46.570 --> 00:00:51.280
Miss Yoshinoya, give me a word you like.

00:00:51.280 --> 00:00:53.530
A word I like?

00:00:53.530 --> 00:00:57.200
Yes. You're young, Miss Yoshinoya,

00:00:57.200 --> 00:01:02.370
so I'm sure you'll be able to choose a word that will stir the hearts of youth.

00:01:02.370 --> 00:01:02.870
Young!

00:01:04.600 --> 00:01:06.080
It has to be "love."

00:01:06.590 --> 00:01:09.910
Love for the arts, love for the students...

00:01:09.910 --> 00:01:18.180
Teaching those cute kids the joy of creating and drawing is love!

00:01:18.540 --> 00:01:21.460
And then there's my love for myself!

00:01:21.460 --> 00:01:22.800
Love is wonderful!

00:01:22.800 --> 00:01:25.200
I'm wonderful!

00:01:25.200 --> 00:01:28.310
Very well, I understand.

00:01:28.750 --> 00:01:31.980
I'll use part of that.

00:01:54.610 --> 00:01:56.050
Morning, Yunocchi.

00:01:56.050 --> 00:01:58.430
Oh, Miya, good morning.

00:01:58.430 --> 00:02:00.290
I'm glad it's sunny today.

00:02:00.290 --> 00:02:03.050
Yeah, we should go shopping.

00:02:03.460 --> 00:02:05.700
Have you started getting ready?

00:02:05.700 --> 00:02:08.420
Nah, I'm gonna start now.

00:02:08.420 --> 00:02:10.480
I hope they like it.

00:02:10.480 --> 00:02:12.980
I'm sure they'll be surprised.

00:02:12.980 --> 00:02:14.900
Yeah.

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:19.900
April 6th

00:02:14.900 --> 00:02:19.900
"Yes/No"

00:02:33.830 --> 00:02:34.780
Yeah?

00:02:34.780 --> 00:02:36.090
Nori!

00:02:36.090 --> 00:02:37.130
Nazuna?

00:02:40.460 --> 00:02:42.010
What's up?

00:02:42.010 --> 00:02:45.650
Um, I got a letter from the others.

00:02:45.650 --> 00:02:46.430
A letter?

00:02:48.180 --> 00:02:51.100
"To Nazuna and Nori,"

00:02:51.100 --> 00:02:54.610
"You are cordially invited to Yuno's room at 5:00 PM today."

00:02:54.610 --> 00:02:56.690
"Bring your appetites."

00:02:56.690 --> 00:02:58.690
"By, the upperclassmen."

00:02:59.280 --> 00:03:00.190
What time is it now?

00:03:00.820 --> 00:03:02.200
4:40.

00:03:02.850 --> 00:03:03.570
Thanks.

00:03:03.570 --> 00:03:07.380
I've gotta get ready. Mind holding on a sec?

00:03:08.370 --> 00:03:09.580
Okay.

00:03:10.700 --> 00:03:14.250
And you don't have to speak so formally with me.

00:03:14.270 --> 00:03:16.210
Okay, Nori...

00:03:18.500 --> 00:03:19.880
It's fine!

00:03:31.350 --> 00:03:34.810
I wonder what they need. It's not like we're that far away.

00:03:34.810 --> 00:03:35.850
Right?

00:03:38.070 --> 00:03:39.370
Hi!

00:03:39.370 --> 00:03:40.610
Sorry to bother...

00:03:42.300 --> 00:03:43.610
...you.

00:03:49.030 --> 00:03:54.750
Um, she said, "It's my fault for eating the strawberries."

00:04:00.500 --> 00:04:03.010
Welcome to Hidamari Apartments!

00:04:03.010 --> 00:04:04.260
Cheers!

00:04:06.760 --> 00:04:10.980
Hey Sae, why don't you start with an explanation of what Hidamari Apartments is?

00:04:11.740 --> 00:04:13.780
You know, the one you gave us last year.

00:04:13.770 --> 00:04:16.400
Oh, um...

00:04:16.400 --> 00:04:21.950
Hidamari Apartments is a small apartment
building right in front of Yamabuki High.

00:04:21.950 --> 00:04:24.900
It's famous for housing a collection of weirdos from the art department.

00:04:25.580 --> 00:04:29.620
But they've all graduated! We're normal now!

00:04:31.330 --> 00:04:33.330
Former occupant of Rm. 201

00:04:33.330 --> 00:04:36.960
All right, first years, eat all you want!

00:04:36.960 --> 00:04:39.170
You're talking pretty big.

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:42.090
Who was it again that ate all the strawberries?

00:04:46.440 --> 00:04:47.840
It's tasty.

00:04:47.840 --> 00:04:50.140
Did you make it yourselves?

00:04:50.140 --> 00:04:52.560
Yeah, we all chipped in.

00:04:52.560 --> 00:04:55.560
Sorry to make you go through all the trouble.

00:04:55.560 --> 00:04:56.980
Sorry.

00:04:56.990 --> 00:04:59.450
Miya, you helped out.

00:04:59.450 --> 00:05:02.440
Did someone do this for you too?

00:05:02.440 --> 00:05:04.190
A welcoming party? Yeah!

00:05:05.620 --> 00:05:07.860
What was it like last year?

00:05:07.860 --> 00:05:11.160
Miya took it like a challenge.

00:05:12.870 --> 00:05:18.460
"To Yuno and Miyako, come to Hiro's room today at 5:00."

00:05:18.460 --> 00:05:20.100
"No tardiness or early starts."

00:05:20.100 --> 00:05:21.790
"By, Sae and Hiro."

00:05:22.280 --> 00:05:25.920
It was written so bravely that I was sure!

00:05:26.990 --> 00:05:28.430
Really?

00:05:28.430 --> 00:05:33.680
We got one too. It seems like a tradition.

00:05:33.680 --> 00:05:34.930
I'm so happy!

00:05:34.930 --> 00:05:36.560
Thanks!

00:05:36.560 --> 00:05:38.190
Don't want to rush you or anything, but...

00:05:38.190 --> 00:05:42.440
Tadah! Behold, Miyako's special talk die!

00:05:43.440 --> 00:05:45.780
You make conversation to match what comes up!

00:05:45.780 --> 00:05:48.200
I'll show you how!

